AN SOUL KNOWS WHAT IS ABOVE ITSELF \(THREE ARTICLES\))>>endobj17577 0 obj<</Parent 17576 0 R/Next 17662 0 R/Dest(FP.Q88.A1)/Title(Article. 1 - Whether the human soul in the present state of life can understand immaterial substances in themselves?)>>endobj17578 0 obj<</Parent 17576 0 R/Dest(FP.Q88.A3)/Prev 17662 0 R/Title(Article. 3 - Whether God is the first object known by the human mind?)>>endobj17579 0 obj<</First 17580 0 R/Parent 17103 0 R/Next 17576 0 R/Dest(FP.Q87)/Count -4/Last 17581 0 R/Prev 17582 0 R/Title(Question. 87 - HOW THE INTELLECTUAL SOUL KNOWS ITSELF AND ALL WITHIN ITSELF \(FOUR ARTICLES\))>>endobj17580 0 obj<</Parent 17579 0 R/Next 17661 0 R/Dest(FP.Q87.A1)/Title(Article. 1 - Whether the intellectual soul knows itself by its essence?)>>endobj17581 0 obj<</Parent 17579 0 R/Dest(FP.Q87.A4)/Prev 17660 0 R/Title(Article. 4 - Whether the intellect understands the act of the will?)>>endobj17582 0 obj<</First 17583 0 R/Parent 17103 0 R/Next 17579 0 R/Dest(FP.Q86)/Count -4/Last 17584 0 R/Prev 17585 0 R/Title(Question. 86 - WHAT OUR INTELLECT KNOWS IN MATERIAL THINGS \(FOUR ARTICLES\))>>endobj17583 0 obj<</Parent 17582 0 R/Next 17659 0 R/Dest(FP.Q86.A1)/Title(Article. 1 - Whether our intellect knows singulars?)>>endobj17584 0 obj<</Parent 17582 0 R/Dest(FP.Q86.A4)/Prev 17658 0 R/Title(Article. 4 - Whether our intellect can know the future?)>>endobj17585 0 obj<</First 17586 0 R/Parent 17103 0 R/Next 17582 0 R/Dest(FP.Q85)/Count -8/Last 17587 0 R/Prev 17588 0 R/Title(Question. 85 - OF THE MODE AND ORDER OF UNDERSTANDING \(EIGHT ARTICLES\))>>endobj17586 0 obj<</Parent 17585 0 R/Next 17657 0 R/Dest(FP.Q85.A1)/Title(Article. 1 - Whether our intellect understands corporeal and material things by abstraction from phantasms?)>>endobj17587 0 obj<</Parent 17585 0 R/Dest(FP.Q85.A8)/Prev 17652 0 R/Title(Article. 8 - Whether the intellect understands the indivisible before the divisible?)>>endobj17588 0 obj<</First 17589 0 R/Parent 17103 0 R/Nex