ful for religious to wear coarser clothes than others?)>>endobj19301 0 obj<</First 19302 0 R/Parent 17092 0 R/Next 19298 0 R/Dest(SS.Q186)/Count -10/Last 19303 0 R/Prev 19304 0 R/Title(Question. 186 - OF THOSE THINGS IN WHICH THE RELIGIOUS STATE PROPERLY CONSISTS \(TEN ARTICLES\))>>endobj19302 0 obj<</Parent 19301 0 R/Next 19329 0 R/Dest(SS.Q186.A1)/Title(Article. 1 - Whether religion implies a state of perfection?)>>endobj19303 0 obj<</Parent 19301 0 R/Dest(SS.Q186.A10)/Prev 19322 0 R/Title(Article. 10 - Whether a religious sins more grievously than a secular by the same kind of sin?)>>endobj19304 0 obj<</First 19305 0 R/Parent 17092 0 R/Next 19301 0 R/Dest(SS.Q185)/Count -8/Last 19306 0 R/Prev 19307 0 R/Title(Question. 185 - OF THINGS PERTAINING TO THE EPISCOPAL STATE \(EIGHT ARTICLES\))>>endobj19305 0 obj<</Parent 19304 0 R/Next 19321 0 R/Dest(SS.Q185.A1)/Title(Article. 1 - Whether it is lawful to desire the office of a bishop?)>>endobj19306 0 obj<</Parent 19304 0 R/Dest(SS.Q185.A8)/Prev 19316 0 R/Title(Article. 8 - Whether religious who are raised to the episcopate are bound to religious observances?)>>endobj19307 0 obj<</First 19308 0 R/Parent 17092 0 R/Next 19304 0 R/Dest(SS.Q184)/Count -8/Last 19309 0 R/Prev 18549 0 R/Title(Question. 184 - OF THE STATE OF PERFECTION IN GENERAL \(EIGHT ARTICLES\))>>endobj19308 0 obj<</Parent 19307 0 R/Next 19315 0 R/Dest(SS.Q184.A1)/Title(Article. 1 - Whether the perfection of the Christian life consists chiefly in charity?)>>endobj19309 0 obj<</Parent 19307 0 R/Dest(SS.Q184.A8)/Prev 19310 0 R/Title(Article. 8 - Whether parish priests and archdeacons are more perfect than religious?)>>endobj19310 0 obj<</Parent 19307 0 R/Next 19309 0 R/Dest(SS.Q184.A7)/Prev 19311 0 R/Title(Article. 7 - Whether the religious state is more perfect than that of prelates?)>>endobj19311 0 obj<</Parent 19307 0 R/Next 19310 0 R/Dest(SS.Q184.A6)/Prev 19312 0 R/Title(Article. 6 - Whether all ecclesiastical prelates are in the state of perfection?)>>endobj19312 0 obj<</Parent 19307 0 R/Next 19311 0 R/Dest(SS.Q184.A5)/Prev 19313 0 R/Title(Article. 5 - Whether religious and prelates are in the state of perfection?)>>endobj19313 0 obj<</Parent 19307 0 R/Next 19312 0 R/Dest(SS.Q184.A4)/Prev 19314 0 R/Title(Article. 4 - Whether whoever is perfect is in the state of perfection?)>>endobj19314 0 obj<</Parent 19307 0 R/Next 19313 0 R/Dest(SS.Q184.A3)/Prev 19315 0 R/Title(Article. 3 - Whether, in this life, perfection consists in the observance of the commandments or of the counsels?)>>endobj19315 0 obj<</Parent 19307 0 R/Next 19314 0 R/Dest(SS.Q184.A2)/Prev 19308 0 R/Title(Article. 2 - Whether any one can be perfect in this life?)>>endobj19316 0 obj<</Parent 19304 0 R/Next 19306 0 R/Dest(SS.Q185.A7)/Prev 19317 0 R/Title(Article. 7 - Whether bishops sin mortally if they distribute not to the poor the ecclesiastical goods which accrue to them?)>>endobj19317 0 obj<</Parent 19304 0 R/Next 19316 0 R/Dest(SS.Q185.A6)/Prev 19318 0 R/Title(Article. 6 - Whether it is lawful for a bishop to have property of his own?)>>endobj19318 0 obj<</Parent 19304 0 R/Next 19317 0 R/Dest(SS.Q185.A5)/Prev 19319 0 R/Title(Article. 5 - Whether it is lawful for a bishop on account of bodily persecution to abandon the flock committed to his care?)>>endobj19319 0 obj<</Parent 19304 0 R/Next 19318 0 R/Dest(SS.Q185.A4)/Prev 19320 0 R/Title(Article. 4 - Whether a bishop may lawfully forsake the episcopal cure, in order to enter religion?)>>endobj19320 0 obj<</Parent 19304 0 R/Next 19319 0 R/Dest(SS.Q185.A3)/Prev 19321 0 R/Title(Article. 3 - Whether he that is appointed to the episcopate ought to be better than others?)>>endobj19321 0 obj<</Parent 19304 0 R/Next 19320 0 R/Dest(SS.Q185.A2)/Prev 19305 0 R/Title(Article. 2 - Whether it is lawful for a man to refuse absolutely an appointment to the episcopate?)>>endobj19322 0 obj<</Parent 19301 0 R/Next 19303 0 R/Dest(SS.Q186.A9)/Prev 19323 0 R/Title(Article. 9 - Whe