d?)>>endobj19939 0 obj<</Parent 19743 0 R/Next 19938 0 R/Dest(TP.Q31.A4)/Prev 19940 0 R/Title(Article. 4 - Whether the matter of Christ's body should have been taken from a woman?)>>endobj19940 0 obj<</Parent 19743 0 R/Next 19939 0 R/Dest(TP.Q31.A3)/Prev 19941 0 R/Title(Article. 3 - Whether Christ's genealogy is suitably traced by the evangelists?)>>endobj19941 0 obj<</Parent 19743 0 R/Next 19940 0 R/Dest(TP.Q31.A2)/Prev 19744 0 R/Title(Article. 2 - Whether Christ took flesh of the seed of David?)>>endobj19942 0 obj<</Parent 19740 0 R/Next 19742 0 R/Dest(TP.Q32.A3)/Prev 19943 0 R/Title(Article. 3 - Whether the Holy Ghost should be called Christ's father in respect of His humanity?)>>endobj19943 0 obj<</Parent 19740 0 R/Next 19942 0 R/Dest(TP.Q32.A2)/Prev 19741 0 R/Title(Article. 2 - Whether it should be said that Christ was conceived of [de] the Holy Ghost?)>>endobj19944 0 obj<</Parent 19737 0 R/Next 19739 0 R/Dest(TP.Q33.A3)/Prev 19945 0 R/Title(Article. 3 - Whether Christ's flesh was first of all conceived and afterwards assumed?)>>endobj19945 0 obj<</Parent 19737 0 R/Next 19944 0 R/Dest(TP.Q33.A2)/Prev 19738 0 R/Title(Article. 2 - Whether Christ's body was animated in the first instant of its conception?)>>endobj19946 0 obj<</Parent 19734 0 R/Next 19736 0 R/Dest(TP.Q34.A3)/Prev 19947 0 R/Title(Article. 3 - Whether Christ could merit in the first instant of His conception?)>>endobj19947 0 obj<</Parent 19734 0 R/Next 19946 0 R/Dest(TP.Q34.A2)/Prev 19735 0 R/Title(Article. 2 - Whether Christ as man had the use of free-will in the first instant of His conception?)>>endobj19948 0 obj<</Parent 19731 0 R/Next 19733 0 R/Dest(TP.Q35.A7)/Prev 19949 0 R/Title(Article. 7 - Whether Christ should have been born in Bethlehem?)>>endobj19949 0 obj<</Parent 19731 0 R/Next 19948 0 R/Dest(TP.Q35.A6)/Prev 19950 0 R/Title(Article. 6 - Whether Christ was born without His Mother suffering?)>>endobj19950 0 obj<</Parent 19731 0 R/Next 19949 0 R/Dest(TP.Q35.A5)/Prev