ed at this renewal?)>>endobj20806 0 obj<</Parent 20783 0 R/Next 20805 0 R/Dest(XP.Q91.A2)/Prev 20784 0 R/Title(Article. 2 - Whether the movement of the heavenly bodies will cease?)>>endobj20807 0 obj<</Parent 20780 0 R/Next 20782 0 R/Dest(XP.Q92.A2)/Prev 20781 0 R/Title(Article. 2 - Whether after the resurrection the saints will see God with the eyes of the body? [*Cf. FP, Q[12], A[3]])>>endobj20808 0 obj<</Parent 20777 0 R/Next 20779 0 R/Dest(XP.Q93.A2)/Prev 20778 0 R/Title(Article. 2 - Whether the degrees of beatitude should be called mansions?)>>endobj20809 0 obj<</Parent 20774 0 R/Next 20776 0 R/Dest(XP.Q94.A2)/Prev 20775 0 R/Title(Article. 2 - Whether the blessed pity the unhappiness of the damned?)>>endobj20810 0 obj<</Parent 20771 0 R/Next 20773 0 R/Dest(XP.Q95.A4)/Prev 20811 0 R/Title(Article. 4 - Whether the angels receive the dowries?)>>endobj20811 0 obj<</Parent 20771 0 R/Next 20810 0 R/Dest(XP.Q95.A3)/Prev 20812 0 R/Title(Article. 3 - Whether it is fitting that Christ should receive a dowry?)>>endobj20812 0 obj<</Parent 20771 0 R/Next 20811 0 R/Dest(XP.Q95.A2)/Prev 20772 0 R/Title(Article. 2 - Whether the dowry is the same as beatitude*? [*Cf. FP, Q[12], A[7], ad 1; FS, Q[4], A[3]])>>endobj20813 0 obj<</Parent 20768 0 R/Next 20770 0 R/Dest(XP.Q96.A12)/Prev 20814 0 R/Title(Article. 12 - Whether the virgin's aureole is the greatest of all?)>>endobj20814 0 obj<</Parent 20768 0 R/Next 20813 0 R/Dest(XP.Q96.A11)/Prev 20815 0 R/Title(Article. 11 - Whether three aureoles are fittingly assigned, those of virgins, of martyrs, and of doctors?)>>endobj20815 0 obj<</Parent 20768 0 R/Next 20814 0 R/Dest(XP.Q96.A10)/Prev 20816 0 R/Title(Article. 10 - Whether an aureole is also due to the body?)>>endobj20816 0 obj<</Parent 20768 0 R/Next 20815 0 R/Dest(XP.Q96.A9)/Prev 20817 0 R/Title(Article. 9 - Whether an aureole is due to the angels?)>>endobj20817 0 obj<</Parent 20768 0 R/Next 20816 0 R/Dest(XP.Q96.A8)/Prev 20818 0 R/Title(Article. 8 - Whethe