 - Whether the damned can make use of the knowledge they had in this world? [*Cf. FP, Q[89]])>>endobj20831 0 obj<</Parent 20762 0 R/Next 20830 0 R/Dest(XP.Q98.A6)/Prev 20832 0 R/Title(Article. 6 - Whether the damned demerit?)>>endobj20832 0 obj<</Parent 20762 0 R/Next 20831 0 R/Dest(XP.Q98.A5)/Prev 20833 0 R/Title(Article. 5 - Whether the damned hate God?)>>endobj20833 0 obj<</Parent 20762 0 R/Next 20832 0 R/Dest(XP.Q98.A4)/Prev 20834 0 R/Title(Article. 4 - Whether in hell the damned would wish others were damned who are not damned?)>>endobj20834 0 obj<</Parent 20762 0 R/Next 20833 0 R/Dest(XP.Q98.A3)/Prev 20835 0 R/Title(Article. 3 - Whether the damned by right and deliberate reason would wish not to be?)>>endobj20835 0 obj<</Parent 20762 0 R/Next 20834 0 R/Dest(XP.Q98.A2)/Prev 20763 0 R/Title(Article. 2 - Whether the damned repent of the evil they have done?)>>endobj20836 0 obj<</Parent 20296 0 R/Next 20761 0 R/Dest(XP.Q99.A4)/Prev 20837 0 R/Title(Article. 4 - Whether the punishment of Christians is brought to an end by the mercy of God?)>>endobj20837 0 obj<</Parent 20296 0 R/Next 20836 0 R/Dest(XP.Q99.A3)/Prev 20838 0 R/Title(Article. 3 - Whether God's mercy suffers at least men to be punished eternally?)>>endobj20838 0 obj<</Parent 20296 0 R/Next 20837 0 R/Dest(XP.Q99.A2)/Prev 20760 0 R/Title(Article. 2 - Whether by God's mercy all punishment of the damned, both men and demons, comes to an end?)>>endobj20839 0 obj<</Parent 20295 0 R/Next 20841 0 R/Dest(XP.Q87.A1)/Title(Article. 1 - Whether after the resurrection every one will know what sins he has committed?)>>endobj20840 0 obj<</Parent 20295 0 R/Dest(XP.Q87.A3)/Prev 20841 0 R/Title(Article. 3 - Whether all merits and demerits, one's own as well as those of others, will be seen by anyone at a single glance?)>>endobj20841 0 obj<</Parent 20295 0 R/Next 20840 0 R/Dest(XP.Q87.A2)/Prev 20839 0 R/Title(Article. 2 - Whether every one will be able to read all that is in another's conscience?)>>en